WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.400
- I don't know if you've
ever noticed this,

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:05.321
but it seems like the more
things that you have to do,

00:00:05.321 --> 00:00:07.020
the harder it is to do
pretty much anything.

00:00:07.020 --> 00:00:10.610
Like you have this long list
of tasks and responsibilities

00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:14.290
that seems to be growing
longer and longer and longer.

00:00:14.290 --> 00:00:16.360
And as it grows in size,

00:00:16.360 --> 00:00:19.830
you also kind of get paralyzed
and intimidated by it.

00:00:19.830 --> 00:00:21.500
Even just thinking about the list

00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:23.080
gives you a mini panic attack.

00:00:23.080 --> 00:00:24.760
And as you mentally go through this list,

00:00:24.760 --> 00:00:26.570
you think to yourself, man,
I don't really need to do

00:00:26.570 --> 00:00:29.150
any of these things like right now.

00:00:29.150 --> 00:00:30.810
I can probably get away with playing

00:00:30.810 --> 00:00:33.320
a little bit of video
games, a little bit of Apex

00:00:33.320 --> 00:00:35.490
because nothing's due right this second.

00:00:35.490 --> 00:00:37.380
And the thing is, you're probably right.

00:00:37.380 --> 00:00:38.930
Most things on that list,

00:00:38.930 --> 00:00:41.280
you don't need to do right this second.

00:00:41.280 --> 00:00:44.180
But the problem is the
longer this list gets,

00:00:44.180 --> 00:00:47.520
the more it subconsciously
affects your wellbeing

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:49.870
and pretty much every aspect of your life.

00:00:49.870 --> 00:00:52.690
You're not able to fall asleep
as fast as you once did.

00:00:52.690 --> 00:00:55.890
Maybe it's graduated
into full blown insomnia.

00:00:55.890 --> 00:00:57.760
Maybe you're plagued
with anxious thoughts,

00:00:57.760 --> 00:01:00.510
like how the hell am I gonna
get all this stuff done?

00:01:00.510 --> 00:01:02.090
What if I don't get any of it done?

00:01:02.090 --> 00:01:03.700
Will I be living on the streets?

00:01:03.700 --> 00:01:06.140
Maybe your entire life has
been played by the fact

00:01:06.140 --> 00:01:09.960
that you can never seem to
just sit down and do work ever.

00:01:09.960 --> 00:01:12.730
You always have a large backlog of things

00:01:12.730 --> 00:01:15.800
that you need to do, and you
are always treading water.

00:01:15.800 --> 00:01:18.700
Maybe you've looked around
at your friends and coworkers

00:01:18.700 --> 00:01:21.050
and wondered how come other people seem

00:01:21.050 --> 00:01:23.290
to be actually able to do stuff?

00:01:23.290 --> 00:01:24.840
Is there something wrong with me?

00:01:24.840 --> 00:01:27.830
So I'm making this video
because those sorts of feelings

00:01:27.830 --> 00:01:30.830
are what has punctuated
my life since birth.

00:01:30.830 --> 00:01:34.120
I know what it's like to
always have something due

00:01:34.120 --> 00:01:36.600
or overdue constantly.

00:01:36.600 --> 00:01:38.440
And it's one of the worst
feelings in the world.

00:01:38.440 --> 00:01:42.326
When you're stressed about
this monumental to-do list

00:01:42.326 --> 00:01:43.159
that you have,

00:01:43.159 --> 00:01:45.520
it's even difficult to
enjoy social outings

00:01:45.520 --> 00:01:47.020
because subconsciously you know

00:01:47.020 --> 00:01:48.840
that you really shouldn't be there.

00:01:48.840 --> 00:01:51.170
You should be tackling this
list of responsibilities.

00:01:51.170 --> 00:01:54.240
It's like a knife in your back
that's slowly being twisted

00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:57.160
as you fake laugh at the jokes
that people make around you.

00:01:57.160 --> 00:01:58.805
It's not fun.

00:01:58.805 --> 00:02:00.410
Luckily though, I've
managed to turn myself

00:02:00.410 --> 00:02:02.930
into a relatively productive human being

00:02:02.930 --> 00:02:05.450
who can actually tackle
the mountain of stuff

00:02:05.450 --> 00:02:07.330
without feeling completely overwhelmed.

00:02:07.330 --> 00:02:09.090
So in this video, I
wanna share with you guys

00:02:09.090 --> 00:02:12.180
my main strategy for tackling
that mountain of stuff

00:02:12.180 --> 00:02:13.420
that we have to do

00:02:13.420 --> 00:02:16.770
and actually gain some
traction in our lives.

00:02:16.770 --> 00:02:17.730
So what's going on here?

00:02:17.730 --> 00:02:19.470
How do we end up in this situation?

00:02:19.470 --> 00:02:21.500
So usually the reason why we end up

00:02:21.500 --> 00:02:23.460
with a mountain of things
that we need to do,

00:02:23.460 --> 00:02:25.140
that we feel overwhelmed by

00:02:25.140 --> 00:02:28.370
is because naturally life
presents itself with tasks

00:02:28.370 --> 00:02:30.440
and responsibilities that we have to do.

00:02:30.440 --> 00:02:31.880
There's no getting around that.

00:02:31.880 --> 00:02:34.830
And these tasks need to
either be done immediately

00:02:34.830 --> 00:02:37.500
or sometime in the not too distant future.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:39.560
If the task isn't utterly urgent,

00:02:39.560 --> 00:02:42.680
what we tend to do is put
it on our backlog of things.

00:02:42.680 --> 00:02:44.480
It's this list that I'm talking about.

00:02:44.480 --> 00:02:46.980
We say, oh, we don't have
to deal with it right now.

00:02:46.980 --> 00:02:48.700
Let's just put it on our to-do list

00:02:48.700 --> 00:02:50.700
and we will tackle it
sometime in the future.

00:02:50.700 --> 00:02:53.060
But this in itself is super problematic

00:02:53.060 --> 00:02:55.820
because almost everything
in life doesn't need

00:02:55.820 --> 00:02:57.660
to be tackled right this second.

00:02:57.660 --> 00:03:00.380
Very few things are immediately urgent

00:03:00.380 --> 00:03:03.600
and require our absolute
attention right this second.

00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:06.710
Which means that 99% of
every task that we get,

00:03:06.710 --> 00:03:07.900
we put on our backlog.

00:03:07.900 --> 00:03:10.380
And since life just naturally dishes out

00:03:10.380 --> 00:03:11.660
these responsibilities,

00:03:11.660 --> 00:03:12.900
we can almost form a graph

00:03:12.900 --> 00:03:15.570
that shows that as time passes along,

00:03:15.570 --> 00:03:18.890
more and more tasks and
responsibilities start to accrue.

00:03:18.890 --> 00:03:22.000
There's also another graph
that's happening simultaneously

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:24.900
that says the more and more
tasks that we have to do,

00:03:24.900 --> 00:03:26.510
the more stress we feel.

00:03:26.510 --> 00:03:28.260
And there's another graph that goes,

00:03:28.260 --> 00:03:31.120
the more stressed out we are
about our current situation,

00:03:31.120 --> 00:03:32.980
the more unpleasant the thought

00:03:32.980 --> 00:03:35.140
of dealing with that situation becomes.

00:03:35.140 --> 00:03:36.250
We have two more left.

00:03:36.250 --> 00:03:38.750
The more unpleasant the
thought of doing anything

00:03:38.750 --> 00:03:40.510
about our situation becomes,

00:03:40.510 --> 00:03:42.060
the more likely we are to escape

00:03:42.060 --> 00:03:43.430
from doing anything about it.

00:03:43.430 --> 00:03:46.220
And finally, the more
likely we are to escape

00:03:46.220 --> 00:03:47.700
from doing anything about it,

00:03:47.700 --> 00:03:50.510
the less likely we are to
actually do anything about it.

00:03:50.510 --> 00:03:52.830
Basically the more time
goes on without dealing

00:03:52.830 --> 00:03:53.870
with our situation,

00:03:53.870 --> 00:03:56.450
the less likely we are
to deal with it anyways.

00:03:56.450 --> 00:03:58.790
And it just becomes this
horrible feedback loop.

00:03:58.790 --> 00:04:00.400
So right about now you're thinking, oh,

00:04:00.400 --> 00:04:03.370
his solution is probably
to just do the things

00:04:03.370 --> 00:04:04.700
before they accrue.

00:04:04.700 --> 00:04:07.000
Do tasks right away, as
soon as you get them.

00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:08.840
And that's actually a great idea,

00:04:08.840 --> 00:04:10.760
but that's not what this video is about.

00:04:10.760 --> 00:04:12.400
That's what my mom would always tell me

00:04:12.400 --> 00:04:13.730
and she's actually right.

00:04:13.730 --> 00:04:16.280
You should just do tasks
pretty much immediately

00:04:16.280 --> 00:04:17.340
after getting them.

00:04:17.340 --> 00:04:19.100
Don't let shit build up basically,

00:04:19.100 --> 00:04:21.450
but that doesn't really
help us if we're already

00:04:21.450 --> 00:04:22.570
in hot water.

00:04:22.570 --> 00:04:25.170
If we're already absolutely
drowning in things

00:04:25.170 --> 00:04:27.820
that we have to do in life
and we need to get out of it.

00:04:27.820 --> 00:04:30.170
And that's where I propose my golden rule,

00:04:30.170 --> 00:04:31.970
do less, not more.

00:04:31.970 --> 00:04:33.830
And you might be thinking
to yourself right now,

00:04:33.830 --> 00:04:35.930
wow, that's a cute quote, Joey,

00:04:35.930 --> 00:04:37.300
you should put that on a poster.

00:04:37.300 --> 00:04:39.150
Unfortunately, that
doesn't make any sense.

00:04:39.150 --> 00:04:40.430
Well, here's the thing,

00:04:40.430 --> 00:04:42.410
it doesn't really make much sense,

00:04:42.410 --> 00:04:44.540
but neither do we as humans.

00:04:44.540 --> 00:04:47.530
We didn't get into this
situation if we made sense,

00:04:47.530 --> 00:04:49.560
if we followed perfect logic.

00:04:49.560 --> 00:04:51.100
If we followed perfect logic,

00:04:51.100 --> 00:04:53.700
we would just do things
as they came to us.

00:04:53.700 --> 00:04:57.300
We would finish off whatever
tasks came up onto our desk

00:04:57.300 --> 00:04:59.430
onto our lap like Santa Claus.

00:04:59.430 --> 00:05:02.320
We got to this situation
because we're highly emotional

00:05:02.320 --> 00:05:03.240
and impulsive.

00:05:03.240 --> 00:05:05.040
When we're in emotional distress,

00:05:05.040 --> 00:05:07.570
we don't respond well
to logical arguments.

00:05:07.570 --> 00:05:10.510
We respond well to momentum and feelings

00:05:10.510 --> 00:05:12.240
of perceived progress.

00:05:12.240 --> 00:05:14.620
So what we should do is
take advantage of this fact

00:05:14.620 --> 00:05:18.190
and leverage our main weakness
and turn it into a strength.

00:05:18.190 --> 00:05:21.090
Every single day, we
have at least one task

00:05:21.090 --> 00:05:22.600
that we know we need to do.

00:05:22.600 --> 00:05:24.500
And if we were to do that thing,

00:05:24.500 --> 00:05:27.970
all other tasks would be
made easier or unnecessary.

00:05:27.970 --> 00:05:31.400
We need to find out what
this task is in our lives.

00:05:31.400 --> 00:05:35.670
And we need to focus our
entire being on completing

00:05:35.670 --> 00:05:36.780
this one thing.

00:05:36.780 --> 00:05:39.660
And we need to pretend
that nothing else exists.

00:05:39.660 --> 00:05:43.140
And with this extra
focus, this unified focus,

00:05:43.140 --> 00:05:46.090
we will be able to complete
this thing in record time.

00:05:46.090 --> 00:05:48.370
Once this one thing is completed,

00:05:48.370 --> 00:05:51.050
then we will feel motivated and energized

00:05:51.050 --> 00:05:53.280
to tackle more things in our lives.

00:05:53.280 --> 00:05:56.790
We will actually feel excited
to keep that momentum going,

00:05:56.790 --> 00:05:59.170
but it's impossible to gain that momentum,

00:05:59.170 --> 00:06:01.460
if we don't tackle that one thing

00:06:01.460 --> 00:06:03.580
and finish it every single day.

00:06:03.580 --> 00:06:05.350
And I'm pretty sure all of us can relate

00:06:05.350 --> 00:06:07.250
to this exact same situation.

00:06:07.250 --> 00:06:10.190
I'm pretty sure we've
all engaged in escapism,

00:06:10.190 --> 00:06:12.480
avoiding that one thing
that we have to do,

00:06:12.480 --> 00:06:15.180
and we escape an escape and
escape until the pressure builds

00:06:15.180 --> 00:06:17.850
and builds and builds, maybe
a deadline is approaching

00:06:17.850 --> 00:06:19.150
and then we just snap out of it.

00:06:19.150 --> 00:06:21.140
We kind of go into survival mode

00:06:21.140 --> 00:06:23.680
and we just tackle that
thing from start to finish

00:06:23.680 --> 00:06:24.620
and we're done.

00:06:24.620 --> 00:06:29.000
And we are so incredibly
relieved and inspired by the fact

00:06:29.000 --> 00:06:31.340
that we did that thing
that we think to ourselves,

00:06:31.340 --> 00:06:33.480
holy smokes, why don't
I just go do more things

00:06:33.480 --> 00:06:34.313
in my life?

00:06:35.296 --> 00:06:36.333
That felt amazing.

00:06:36.333 --> 00:06:38.610
And that's the exact emotion
that we're trying to tap into.

00:06:38.610 --> 00:06:42.600
It's that feeling of having
completed a very important thing

00:06:42.600 --> 00:06:45.780
and then leveraging that
momentum to tackle more things.

00:06:45.780 --> 00:06:47.610
And I think we can only get to that point,

00:06:47.610 --> 00:06:49.450
if we kind of put the blinders on

00:06:49.450 --> 00:06:52.300
and forget about literally
everything else on our list.

00:06:52.300 --> 00:06:55.410
We use our emotional compass
to figure out which thing has

00:06:55.410 --> 00:06:57.500
the most emotional resistance.

00:06:57.500 --> 00:06:59.540
What thing are we avoiding the most?

00:06:59.540 --> 00:07:02.300
That is likely to be not guaranteed to be,

00:07:02.300 --> 00:07:04.510
the most important thing
that you have to do

00:07:04.510 --> 00:07:05.440
in any given day.

00:07:05.440 --> 00:07:08.090
For me, as I've talked
about in other videos,

00:07:08.090 --> 00:07:09.650
that thing is writing.

00:07:09.650 --> 00:07:12.960
Writing by far has the most
emotional resistance for me.

00:07:12.960 --> 00:07:16.370
I don't really like doing
it, but once I have done it,

00:07:16.370 --> 00:07:18.500
then I have content to work with.

00:07:18.500 --> 00:07:20.830
I have something to film,
I have something to edit

00:07:20.830 --> 00:07:22.510
and I have something to upload.

00:07:22.510 --> 00:07:26.100
Writing is kind of the backbone
of my entire YouTube career.

00:07:26.100 --> 00:07:28.010
It's the most important thing

00:07:28.010 --> 00:07:29.810
that I can do in any given day.

00:07:29.810 --> 00:07:31.450
As long as I continue writing,

00:07:31.450 --> 00:07:33.120
I can continue YouTubing.

00:07:33.120 --> 00:07:35.660
Maybe your life is really
consistent like mine,

00:07:35.660 --> 00:07:37.180
or maybe it's super turbulent

00:07:37.180 --> 00:07:41.010
and that one thing will change
on a daily or weekly basis.

00:07:41.010 --> 00:07:42.260
You now take what I'm saying

00:07:42.260 --> 00:07:45.420
and apply it directly to
your life and your needs.

00:07:45.420 --> 00:07:47.150
Right now, you probably have something

00:07:47.150 --> 00:07:48.760
that you know you need to do,

00:07:48.760 --> 00:07:50.710
and you're really resisting doing it.

00:07:50.710 --> 00:07:53.350
Maybe you've been resisting
it for a long time.

00:07:53.350 --> 00:07:57.130
That's your one thing, do not
worry about anything else,

00:07:57.130 --> 00:07:58.250
complete that thing.

00:07:58.250 --> 00:07:59.970
And once you complete that thing,

00:07:59.970 --> 00:08:02.380
the answer and the motivation and energy,

00:08:02.380 --> 00:08:05.170
you need to complete everything
else will be provided

00:08:05.170 --> 00:08:06.500
for you in droves.

00:08:06.500 --> 00:08:09.390
Putting the blinders on and
forgetting every other task,

00:08:09.390 --> 00:08:13.190
except the one thing also
adds clarity to the overwhelm.

00:08:13.190 --> 00:08:15.190
It brings order to the chaos.

00:08:15.190 --> 00:08:17.624
Our brain can stop bird
shotting everywhere

00:08:17.624 --> 00:08:19.630
and thinking about a
million things at once

00:08:19.630 --> 00:08:23.120
and getting super worried,
just calm your brain down,

00:08:23.120 --> 00:08:25.530
focus on completing the one thing.

00:08:25.530 --> 00:08:28.530
Take everything that you
need to do and write it down.

00:08:28.530 --> 00:08:30.980
Write down every task
that you can think of

00:08:30.980 --> 00:08:33.690
onto a piece of paper and try to identify

00:08:33.690 --> 00:08:35.950
the most important thing
that you need to do.

00:08:35.950 --> 00:08:39.220
And then what I want you to
do is circle that one thing

00:08:39.220 --> 00:08:41.200
and scribble out everything else.

00:08:41.200 --> 00:08:42.590
Don't worry about anything else,

00:08:42.590 --> 00:08:45.410
give yourself a mental
vacation from everything else.

00:08:45.410 --> 00:08:46.910
Do that one thing.

00:08:46.910 --> 00:08:48.760
It's the only thing that exists.

00:08:48.760 --> 00:08:51.770
And whether you are
excited to do it or not,

00:08:51.770 --> 00:08:53.550
it doesn't matter, submit to it.

00:08:53.550 --> 00:08:57.610
Submit to just doing it,
starting it, completing it,

00:08:57.610 --> 00:08:59.080
not a big deal, do it.

00:08:59.080 --> 00:09:00.650
'Cause if you have to do it anyways,

00:09:00.650 --> 00:09:03.300
there's no point in getting
all emotionally worked up

00:09:03.300 --> 00:09:04.794
about it.

00:09:04.794 --> 00:09:05.627
You just have mental clarity.

00:09:05.627 --> 00:09:07.610
You submit to the fact
that you have to do it.

00:09:07.610 --> 00:09:09.390
You do it without resistance,

00:09:09.390 --> 00:09:11.130
you do it without hyping yourself up

00:09:11.130 --> 00:09:14.840
and once you complete it,
you'll feel calmly empowered

00:09:14.840 --> 00:09:17.763
to restore more order into your life.

00:09:19.060 --> 00:09:22.860
This video was inspired by
The One Thing by Gary Keller.

